-- title:
--   Root distance controlled along one path
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a convex subset of a real normed space and consider an ordered tree with positive edge weights $w(c)$ summing to $1$ over each parent's children, path weights $\pi_k(v)$, and nonexpansive node maps $f_{k,v}:K\to K$. The tree is evaluated bottom-up: for values $H$ at level $k+1$, $\mathrm{collapse}(H)(p)=f_{k,p}\bigl(\sum_{\mathrm{par}(c)=p}w(c)H(c)\bigr)$, and $\mathrm{ev}_k(H)$ iterates collapse up to the root. Assume $\operatorname{diam}K\le1$. For a cutoff assignment $H$ at level $k$, a node $v$ there and $z\in K$,
--   $$
--   \|\mathrm{ev}_k(H)-z\|\le\pi_k(v)\|H(v)-z\|+(1-\pi_k(v))+\sum_{u\text{ proper anc. of }v}\pi(u)\,\|f_u(z)-z\| .
--   $$
--
--   Only the focused path matters; everything else costs at most its mass.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Nonexpansive/BlockBefore.lean#L117-L147

